-- title:
--   Unordered endpoint key of an event
-- statement:
--   For an ordered endpoint event on $n$ positions, assign the unordered pair of its endpoints. Reversing the endpoints gives the same key, and repeated endpoints are permitted. The key is an element of the symmetric square rather than a two element subset, so diagonal pairs are retained. It provides an orientation independent representation when selecting or counting event edges.
